cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below (and cite the R packages meta and metafor, whose methods it re-implements)."
type: software
title: "MetaJava: meta-analysis in Java following the R packages meta and metafor"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/tarak-dhaouadi/metajava"
url: "https://github.com/tarak-dhaouadi/metajava"
abstract: >-
  A stand-alone desktop application (Java Swing, no R needed) for meta-analysis:
  binary, continuous, correlation, generic, incidence-rate, single-mean,
  single-proportion and single-rate data; common-effect and random-effects
  models with the tau-squared estimators, confidence-interval and prediction-interval
  methods of the R package meta; subgroup analysis, meta-regression, leave-one-out
  and cumulative analyses, publication-bias tests and trim-and-fill, forest, funnel,
  bubble, Baujat and radial plots, and the outlier and influence diagnostics of metafor.
keywords:
  - meta-analysis
  - forest plot
  - prediction interval
  - heterogeneity
  - meta-regression
  - influence diagnostics
  - Java
authors:
